  "text_to_speech": "fungi have complex life cycles consisting of asexual and sexual reproductive phases here we examine the life cycle of the black bread mold Raisa post alone affirm the black speckles that rise applause producers on bread are capsules called sporangia that the fungus produces through asexual reproduction the fungus consists of a network of filaments called hyphy that penetrate the bread and absorb nutrients during asexual reproduction spore filled sporangia develop at the tops of stock like hyphy the sporangia and - are haploid sporangia break open and they're haploid spores disseminate sports travel by air to other locations and may land on suitable food sources such as a flaky croissant a spore germinates and sends an elongated Haifa into the croissant to absorb nutrients as it develops the new haploid fungus can produce more sporangia initiating additional cycles of asexual reproduction in addition to asexual reproduction the fungus may initiate sexual reproduction although rhizopus does not have two distinct sexes it does have two distinct mating types designated plus and minus they reproduce sexually when adjacent hyphy of the two types release pheromones the pheromones trigger the hyphy to grow side branches note that raisa puss generally lacks cross walls between its nuclei and most nuclei share a common cytoplasm as the side branches grow nuclei stream in across wall forms near the end of each branch isolating several haploid nuclei at the ends the nuclei are now isolated in sexual structures called gamma tangia these gamma tangia fuse and the nuclei inside pair up the parents of nuclei eventually fuse as well and the entire multinucleate structure becomes as I go sporangium the Zygo sporangium develops a thick tough wall and can remain dormant for months the diploid nuclei within the Sango sporangia then undergo meiosis and a sporangia m-- sprouts the sporangia maintains the products of meiosis haploid nuclei that are incorporated into spores when the sporangium opens these spores will disperse and germinate to form the next generation of haploid hyphy",
  "text_to_speech_word_count": 335,
  "timecoded_text_to_speech": [
    {
      "end": "00:00:08.750",
      "start": "00:00:00.000",
      "text": " Fun Gi have complex life cycles consisting of asexual and sexual reproductive phases."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:14.167",
      "start": "00:00:08.750",
      "text": " Here, we examine the life cycle of the black bread mold, rhizopostolonefer."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:19.750",
      "start": "00:00:14.167",
      "text": " The black speckles that rhizopost producers on bread are capsules called sporangia that"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:24.250",
      "start": "00:00:19.750",
      "text": " the fungus produces through asexual reproduction."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:29.500",
      "start": "00:00:24.250",
      "text": " The fungus consists of a network of filaments called hyphae that penetrate the bread and"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:31.667",
      "start": "00:00:29.500",
      "text": " absorb nutrients."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:37.917",
      "start": "00:00:31.667",
      "text": " During asexual reproduction, sporfilts sporangia develop at the tops of stock like hyphae."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:41.250",
      "start": "00:00:37.917",
      "text": " The sporangia and hyphae are haploid."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:45.917",
      "start": "00:00:41.250",
      "text": " Sporangia break open and their haploid spores disseminate."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:50.750",
      "start": "00:00:45.917",
      "text": " Spores travel by air to other locations and may land on suitable food sources such as"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:52.583",
      "start": "00:00:50.750",
      "text": " a flaky quassant."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:58.583",
      "start": "00:00:52.583",
      "text": " A spore germinates and sends an elongated hypha into the quassant to absorb nutrients."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:03.833",
      "start": "00:00:58.583",
      "text": " As it develops, the new haploid fungus can produce more sporangia, initiating additional"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:07.500",
      "start": "00:01:03.833",
      "text": " cycles of asexual reproduction."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:13.083",
      "start": "00:01:07.500",
      "text": " In addition to asexual reproduction, the fungus may initiate sexual reproduction."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:19.000",
      "start": "00:01:13.083",
      "text": " Although rhizopost does not have two distinct sexes, it does have two distinct mating types,"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:21.417",
      "start": "00:01:19.000",
      "text": " designated plus and minus."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:27.167",
      "start": "00:01:21.417",
      "text": " They reproduce sexually when adjacent hyphae of the two types release pheromones."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:30.917",
      "start": "00:01:27.167",
      "text": " The pheromones trigger the hyphae to grow side branches."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:36.083",
      "start": "00:01:30.917",
      "text": " Note that rhizopost generally lacks cross walls between its nuclei and most nuclei share"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:38.500",
      "start": "00:01:36.083",
      "text": " a common cytoplasm."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:41.833",
      "start": "00:01:38.500",
      "text": " As the side branches grow, nuclei stream in."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:48.917",
      "start": "00:01:41.833",
      "text": " A cross wall forms near the end of each branch, isolating several haploid nuclei at the ends."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:53.750",
      "start": "00:01:48.917",
      "text": " The nuclei are now isolated in sexual structures called gamutangia."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:57.917",
      "start": "00:01:53.750",
      "text": " These gamutangia fuse and the nuclei inside pair up."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:02:03.750",
      "start": "00:01:57.917",
      "text": " The pairs of nuclei eventually fuse as well, and the entire multi-nucleate structure becomes"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:02:05.917",
      "start": "00:02:03.750",
      "text": " a zygosporangium."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:02:11.833",
      "start": "00:02:05.917",
      "text": " The zygosporangium develops a thick, tough wall and can remain dormant for months."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:02:18.833",
      "start": "00:02:11.833",
      "text": " The diploid nuclei within the zygosporangium then undergo meiosis, and the sporangium sprouts."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:02:25.750",
      "start": "00:02:18.833",
      "text": " The sporangium contains the products of meiosis, haploid nuclei that are incorporated into spores."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:02:31.000",
      "start": "00:02:25.750",
      "text": " When the sporangium opens, these spores will disperse and germinate to form the next generation"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:02:32.000",
      "start": "00:02:31.000",
      "text": " of haploid hyphae."
    }
  ],
